{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1468, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an array original of length n and a 2D array bounds of length n x 2, where bounds[i] = [u_i, v_i].\nYou need to find the number of possible arrays copy of length n such that:\n\n(copy[i] - copy[i - 1]) == (original[i] - original[i - 1]) for 1 <= i <= n - 1.\nu_i <= copy[i] <= v_i for 0 <= i <= n - 1.\n\nReturn the number of such arrays.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: original = [1,2,3,4], bounds = [[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5]]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nThe possible arrays are:\n\n[1, 2, 3, 4]\n[2, 3, 4, 5]\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: original = [1,2,3,4], bounds = [[1,10],[2,9],[3,8],[4,7]]\nOutput: 4\nExplanation:\nThe possible arrays are:\n\n[1, 2, 3, 4]\n[2, 3, 4, 5]\n[3, 4, 5, 6]\n[4, 5, 6, 7]\n\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: original = [1,2,1,2], bounds = [[1,1],[2,3],[3,3],[2,3]]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation:\nNo array is possible.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n2 <= n == original.length <= 10^5\n1 <= original[i] <= 10^9\nbounds.length == n\nbounds[i].length == 2\n1 <= bounds[i][0] <= bounds[i][1] <= 10^9\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def countArrays(self, original: List[int], bounds: List[List[int]]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1542, "char_start": 1480, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 3, 4]\n[[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [4, 5]]\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1617, "char_start": 1554, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 3, 4]\n[[1, 10], [2, 9], [3, 8], [4, 7]]\nOutput:\n4", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1691, "char_start": 1629, "quote": "Input:\n[1, 2, 1, 2]\n[[1, 1], [2, 3], [3, 3], [2, 3]]\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "9ef3759aa7b69e14a0503c34e6f6c845ac6d40ab5eb358a0ca44dbc1c568aa2c", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "8d97e13437b03c63304cb283e709456df9bf902bd3d361487104d8763faed9dc", "seq": 2}
